WEBVTT

00:01.700 --> 00:05.053
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.153 --> 00:08.438
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.522 --> 00:11.923
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.974 --> 00:14.892
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.959 --> 00:18.476
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.561 --> 00:21.679
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.746 --> 00:23.279
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.364 --> 00:24.730
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.781 --> 00:26.189
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:31.251 --> 00:34.168
Hello, I'm Brian Griffin.
And I'm Stewie Griffin.

00:34.236 --> 00:36.936
A few years ago, we did an
episode called "Viewer Mail"

00:37.004 --> 00:39.504
where you, our fans,
wrote in and suggested ideas

00:39.572 --> 00:41.122
for new episodes.

00:41.190 --> 00:43.957
Well, it's ten years later, but
you're still sending in ideas.

00:44.024 --> 00:46.692
Uh, to Rashad in Little Rock,
we wanna let you know

00:46.759 --> 00:50.343
we kicked around idea, "Make the
Baby Go Wild" for a while,

00:50.410 --> 00:52.462
couldn't really find
an angle on it.

00:52.546 --> 00:54.730
Here's one from
Lee Mills of Iowa.

00:54.797 --> 00:57.631
<i>Lee writes: "Dear Family Guy,
was your show based on anything?"</i>

00:57.699 --> 00:59.348
That's a great question, Lee.

00:59.416 --> 01:02.182
In fact, Family Guy is based
on an American television series

01:02.250 --> 01:04.151
<i>called The Simpsons.</i>

01:04.218 --> 01:07.302
<i>(chuckles) Actually, Family Guy,
much like The Office,</i>

01:07.387 --> 01:09.420
<i>is based on a British series
called Chap of the Manor.</i>

01:09.488 --> 01:10.837
Let's watch.

01:14.139 --> 01:15.974
(farting)

01:19.010 --> 01:20.542
<i>ANNOUNCER:
We now return to Britain's</i>

01:20.610 --> 01:22.243
<i>most popular game show...</i>

01:22.311 --> 01:25.713
<i>BRITISH AUDIENCE:
Wheel... of... Politeness!</i>

01:25.780 --> 01:27.480
Do go ahead, then.
Oh, no, you first.

01:27.548 --> 01:29.448
Wouldn't dream of it.
Too kind, really, I insist.

01:29.515 --> 01:31.515
Wouldn't be proper of me.
I appreciate your courtesy.

01:31.583 --> 01:32.782
Likewise.
Well, we're all out of time.

01:32.849 --> 01:34.283
Join us same time tomorrow

01:34.351 --> 01:36.317
if it's not entirely
inconvenient for you.

01:36.385 --> 01:37.686
If so, of course,
we do understand

01:37.754 --> 01:39.486
and we do apologize in advance.

01:39.554 --> 01:42.221
This has all been an imposition.
I'm so dreadfully sorry.

01:42.289 --> 01:43.021
Sorry! Sorry.
Sorry.

01:43.089 --> 01:44.222
Sorry, everyone!

01:44.290 --> 01:45.922
All right, kids, enough telly.

01:45.990 --> 01:48.458
I hope everyone's peckish
for some boiled lamb shank.

01:48.525 --> 01:49.759
None for me, Lydia.

01:49.827 --> 01:51.425
I'm meeting me mates
down at the pub.

01:51.493 --> 01:53.777
Again? But Neville,
you spend all your time

01:53.828 --> 01:56.378
down at the Fox and Pig
and Dog and Wolf and Cat

01:56.446 --> 01:57.545
and Fiddle and
Whistle and Cock.

01:57.613 --> 01:58.896
And that's where
you're wrong.

01:58.964 --> 02:01.031
The Fox and Pig and Dog
and Wolf and Cat

02:01.115 --> 02:02.949
and Fiddle and Whistle and Cock
is for tossers.

02:03.000 --> 02:05.200
We're meetin' at the Dog and Cat
and Bull and Whistle

02:05.267 --> 02:07.201
and Fiddle and Cock
and Pig and Wolf and Carriage

02:07.268 --> 02:08.735
and Fife and Other Wolf!

02:08.802 --> 02:11.253
But I need you to stay and have
a chat with Collingsworth.

02:11.321 --> 02:13.454
I found him with another fag
in his mouth this morning.

02:13.522 --> 02:14.789
Oh, is that right?

02:14.856 --> 02:16.722
So you fancy fags, do you?

02:16.790 --> 02:19.257
Well, here.
Have a whole carton of fags!

02:19.325 --> 02:22.342
I just want a comely lass
to look upon me with favour.

02:22.427 --> 02:23.843
I look on you with favour.

02:23.910 --> 02:25.493
I look on all of you
with favour.

02:25.561 --> 02:27.062
Shut up, British Meg.

02:27.129 --> 02:28.162
(Texas accent)
Look at Lydia.

02:28.229 --> 02:30.729
What a two-bit Wichita whore.

02:30.797 --> 02:33.031
<i>One of these days,
she's gonna wake up killt.</i>

02:33.099 --> 02:34.499
Ah, matricide.

02:34.567 --> 02:36.533
Yet another of
your childhood whims.

02:36.600 --> 02:38.267
No, it ain't. I'm gonna follow
through with...

02:38.335 --> 02:39.568
Wait, why'd you say it
like that?

02:40.836 --> 02:42.536
Cutaway, sir?

02:42.603 --> 02:44.638
Yes, that's good then.

02:44.706 --> 02:47.539
Friends, family,
and characters random

02:47.606 --> 02:50.373
To bring you joy
and laughter in tandem

02:50.441 --> 02:53.208
To divert and dazzle
is our intention

02:53.276 --> 02:56.527
So sit back, relax,
and enjoy our invention.

02:59.146 --> 03:01.562
Ah, I love summer.

03:10.136 --> 03:12.602
Good evening, Billingsbury.
I'm Clive Crowley.

03:12.670 --> 03:15.137
Coming up: a man with a gun
and two bullets

03:15.203 --> 03:17.305
has taken over the city
of Manchester.

03:17.373 --> 03:20.040
But first, our top story
tonight: Her Majesty, the Queen,

03:20.107 --> 03:22.341
will be passing through
our very town tomorrow.

03:22.409 --> 03:24.275
With details, we now go live

03:24.343 --> 03:26.242
to Indian reporter,
Tricia Dasgupta.

03:26.309 --> 03:28.978
Oh, my golly,
there is much commotion.

03:29.046 --> 03:30.645
Thank you, Tricia.
After the interval,

03:30.713 --> 03:33.513
find out which 12 football teams
tied tonight.

03:33.580 --> 03:35.447
The Queen's comin'
to Billingsbury?

03:35.515 --> 03:37.148
That's bloody sweet!

03:37.215 --> 03:39.283
You know, I'm actually a
relation of the royal family.

03:39.351 --> 03:41.151
You most certainly are not.

03:41.218 --> 03:42.951
Where would you
get that idea?

03:43.019 --> 03:44.952
Me mum used to claim
she was a Windsor.

03:45.020 --> 03:47.853
And I always heard my Nana talk
about how she took a duke.

03:47.921 --> 03:49.455
Must've been a difficult
marriage, too,

03:49.522 --> 03:51.222
'cause every afternoon
she'd be belly-achin'

03:51.290 --> 03:52.790
about her bloody duke.

03:52.857 --> 03:54.925
I think you just had
a gross grandmother.

03:54.993 --> 03:57.192
No, I'm quite sure of it.
And to prove it,

03:57.260 --> 03:59.226
I'm gonna nick
one of the Queen's hairs

03:59.294 --> 04:00.844
during her visit tomorrow.

04:00.911 --> 04:03.796
And when the DNA proves a match,
you'll see I'm royalty.

04:03.863 --> 04:05.263
The Queen, eh?

04:05.330 --> 04:07.465
I'd like to mash my banger
in her blood pudding.

04:07.533 --> 04:08.564
Googity. Googity. Glop.

04:08.648 --> 04:10.782
Hello, lads.
Oh, hello, Seamus.

04:10.850 --> 04:13.218
Right fine performance
at the cricket match today.

04:13.285 --> 04:16.285
Aye. I was spirited to have you
down there watching me.

04:16.353 --> 04:18.153
P.A. ANNOUNCER:
Well, it's a brilliant day

04:18.221 --> 04:19.421
for a long and
confusing game of cricket.

04:19.489 --> 04:21.454
The field is teeming
with men in helmets

04:21.522 --> 04:23.122
who don't seem like
they need helmets,

04:23.189 --> 04:24.691
and men not in helmets

04:24.759 --> 04:26.158
who seem like they probably
should be wearing helmets.

04:26.225 --> 04:29.126
Oh, he's batted it
clear out of the stadium.

04:29.193 --> 04:32.627
Is that good? We don't know,
but it's what we do!

04:32.695 --> 04:34.028
Y-Yay!

04:34.095 --> 04:34.963
Boo!
Boo!

04:35.031 --> 04:35.963
Boo!

04:39.199 --> 04:42.083
Oh my goodness, the Queen is
going to be here presently.

04:42.150 --> 04:43.917
This is oh-so-exciting!

04:43.984 --> 04:46.151
My favorite part
before the Queen arrives

04:46.219 --> 04:48.920
is yelling "wanker"
at Prince Charles as he passes.

04:49.004 --> 04:50.337
Wanker!
Wanker!

04:50.404 --> 04:52.071
I know, I know.

04:52.122 --> 04:53.371
Wanker!
Wanker!

04:53.422 --> 04:55.238
Yes, I know. Yes.

04:55.290 --> 04:56.757
Wanker!
You're a wanker!

04:56.841 --> 04:58.674
Wanker!
Right, quite right.

04:58.742 --> 05:00.292
Spot on. He's got it.

05:00.359 --> 05:03.044
I say, a lot of people have
turned out to see the Queen.

05:03.111 --> 05:04.412
Should make for a grand day.

05:04.478 --> 05:07.262
Hey, watch it there!

05:15.618 --> 05:17.468
Good show, old chap.
Well played.

05:17.534 --> 05:18.601
Here she comes!

05:18.685 --> 05:20.103
(crowd cheering)

05:22.372 --> 05:24.088
Very well.
Time for action.

05:24.156 --> 05:27.290
A lock of the Queen's hair
shall soon be mine.

05:27.358 --> 05:29.108
Here she comes.
Have at it then.

05:29.175 --> 05:32.160
Crikey! This is a haircut
fit for a queen!

05:35.112 --> 05:36.444
Oh, bloody hell!

05:36.512 --> 05:38.512
All right, time for Plan B.
Let's go!

05:45.934 --> 05:47.751
I'm not going any lower.

05:47.818 --> 05:49.701
Well, Father,
you gave it a good go.

05:49.769 --> 05:52.602
Oh, we're not done yet.
Come on!

05:52.653 --> 05:54.205
(tires squeal)

05:54.272 --> 05:57.489
Queen! Queen! Give me
some of your hair!

05:57.573 --> 05:59.574
Come on, Queen!
Don't be a bitch!

05:59.625 --> 06:01.290
Get us away
from that lunatic!

06:01.375 --> 06:02.758
(tires squeal)

06:11.581 --> 06:13.047
She's heading into that tunnel!

06:14.482 --> 06:17.716
(crashing, horse neighs)

06:17.784 --> 06:20.584
GUARD (screaming):
Dear God! The Queen's dead!

06:20.652 --> 06:23.586
(both whistling)

06:23.637 --> 06:25.786
All right, Collingsworth,
I got a hair.

06:25.837 --> 06:29.306
Now, just walk away casual-like
and we're in the clear.

06:29.391 --> 06:30.924
Oh, no!
Here come the coppers!

06:30.991 --> 06:34.425
("Yakkity Sax" playing)

06:40.746 --> 06:43.147
(inhales deeply)

06:43.214 --> 06:44.480
Bugger.

06:44.548 --> 06:46.715
(inhales deeply)

06:46.783 --> 06:48.349
Bugger.

06:48.416 --> 06:50.384
(inhales deeply)

06:50.452 --> 06:51.551
Bugger.

06:54.821 --> 06:56.953
Well, it turns out
I'm not royalty.

06:57.021 --> 06:58.687
Shame about the Queen, though.

06:58.755 --> 07:01.190
Yeah, I reckon she's with
Jesus Christ in heaven now.

07:01.258 --> 07:02.590
(spits)
(metallic ding)

07:02.658 --> 07:04.641
Well, I'm just happy our
family is safe and sound

07:04.709 --> 07:06.843
back in our cozy row house.

07:06.910 --> 07:08.210
Row house.

07:14.201 --> 07:16.091
(thunder rumbling)

07:16.092 --> 07:17.491
TV ANNOUNCER:
We now return

07:17.559 --> 07:19.443
<i>to The Comedy Central Roast
of Robin Williams.</i>

07:19.511 --> 07:21.628
Aw, man, Robin Williams
is my favorite!

07:21.695 --> 07:23.061
He must be getting recognized

07:23.129 --> 07:24.763
for all his contributions
to show business.

07:24.831 --> 07:26.364
I don't think
that's what a roast is.

07:26.431 --> 07:29.365
Robin, as a comic, it's an honor
to be up here roasting you.

07:29.432 --> 07:31.599
As a moviegoer, I want
to punch you in the face.

07:31.667 --> 07:33.234
(laughter)

07:33.302 --> 07:35.167
Oh, that's funny.
Advocate violence.

07:35.235 --> 07:36.535
And let's face it, Mork.

07:36.603 --> 07:38.603
You're getting Nanu-Na-old!

07:38.671 --> 07:40.570
(laughs)
(laughter)

07:40.638 --> 07:42.271
Stop it! You stop it!

07:42.338 --> 07:45.907
Robin Williams has a manic gift
that gladdens a sad world

07:45.975 --> 07:49.842
and all he asks in return
is our unceasing attention!

07:49.909 --> 07:51.743
How can you allow this?!

07:51.795 --> 07:54.761
Robin Williams has given us
nothing but joy!

07:54.845 --> 07:57.214
I wish everyone
was Robin Williams!

07:57.265 --> 07:59.580
(thunder rumbling)
(electric sizzling)

08:01.132 --> 08:03.582
Boy, that looks enticing.

08:03.634 --> 08:05.100
(thunder rumbling)
(electric sizzling)

08:05.184 --> 08:08.436
Yeah, this is nice.

08:13.138 --> 08:15.405
Oh, my God.
What happened?

08:15.473 --> 08:18.324
You were in a coma, and then I
kissed you, and you woke up.

08:18.392 --> 08:19.858
(mumbles)
Like two days later.

08:19.925 --> 08:21.893
Anyway, all your
numbers are normal.

08:21.944 --> 08:23.394
What numbers?
No idea.

08:23.461 --> 08:26.361
Well, congratulations.
You're gonna be just fine.

08:26.429 --> 08:27.895
(electric buzzing)

08:27.963 --> 08:29.414
Oh, my God!

08:29.482 --> 08:30.864
You're...
You're Robin Williams!

08:30.931 --> 08:33.499
Ding! Thank you for playing
"That's Obvious!"

08:33.566 --> 08:34.866
Tell him what he's won, Cletus!

08:34.933 --> 08:36.067
(hick accent): Money!
(normal): Ho-ho! Money.

08:36.135 --> 08:37.050
Or as the Republicans
call it,

08:37.118 --> 08:38.067
(imitating witch):
Mine!

08:38.118 --> 08:39.568
(laughs)

08:39.636 --> 08:41.270
I hope this is covered
by your HMO.

08:41.338 --> 08:43.337
I was covered once by
an HMO in San Francisco.

08:43.405 --> 08:45.605
I Haight my Ashbury
in these jeans!

08:45.673 --> 08:47.272
Ding-ding, Rice-A-Roni!

08:47.340 --> 08:50.373
Ah! You got all those
references in there!

08:50.441 --> 08:51.809
Of course now everyone
can afford health care

08:51.877 --> 08:52.776
because of Obama.

08:52.843 --> 08:54.377
Yeah, you want a Band-Aid?

08:54.445 --> 08:57.111
No problem, turkey.
Come on down to Obama-Mart!

08:57.179 --> 08:59.579
The price is free,
but yo ass better vote for me.

08:59.647 --> 09:01.380
Ha! Political
with a twist.

09:01.448 --> 09:02.947
It's funny from the news!

09:02.998 --> 09:04.998
What's going on in here?
You gotta check this out!

09:05.083 --> 09:06.300
It's Robin Williams!

09:06.368 --> 09:08.050
Ho-ho! A nurse
is a nurse, of curse.

09:08.117 --> 09:10.284
Up yours, Wilbur.

09:10.335 --> 09:11.669
Oh, my God!

09:11.737 --> 09:13.938
Everyone I touch
turns into Robin Williams!

09:14.005 --> 09:16.472
Yess! Peter Sweet Cheeks
Griffin-uh!

09:16.539 --> 09:19.190
You have been given
the power from god-uh!

09:19.258 --> 09:20.190
Ho-ho! Ho-ho!
Ho-ho!

09:20.258 --> 09:22.674
(laughing)

09:22.742 --> 09:25.543
I will be so responsible
with this.

09:25.611 --> 09:27.010
Thanks, guys!

09:27.078 --> 09:28.461
Ho-ho!
Bye!

09:28.512 --> 09:30.462
See you, Peter!
Y'all come back now, y'hear?

09:30.513 --> 09:31.897
<i>(chuckles)
It's Patch Adams Robin.</i>

09:31.964 --> 09:34.447
He cures stuff the fun way,
not the medicine way.

09:37.951 --> 09:40.317
So, somehow the lightning
gave your dad

09:40.385 --> 09:43.152
the power to turn anyone
I touch into Robin Williams.

09:43.220 --> 09:45.986
Peter, did Dr. Hartman say
how long this was gonna last?

09:46.054 --> 09:47.421
There is no more
Dr. Hartman, Lois.

09:47.489 --> 09:49.223
He's Robin Williams now.

09:49.290 --> 09:50.623
Bet you kids never thought
your dad

09:50.691 --> 09:52.806
would have superpowers, huh?

09:52.858 --> 09:55.592
Peter!
Ho-ho! You pat my back, I pat yours,

09:55.659 --> 09:57.192
and Pat Robertson
pats Mr. Happy.

09:57.260 --> 09:59.694
(Southern accent): Yayuss! Praise
Jesus with your Visa card!

09:59.762 --> 10:01.529
Max it out
on the Lord, people!

10:01.597 --> 10:02.896
Oh, boy!

10:02.964 --> 10:05.130
And that's the second
Southern preacher one.

10:05.197 --> 10:06.798
Look, Brian! Meg is
one of the sensitive,

10:06.866 --> 10:08.432
bearded Robin Williams
characters.

10:08.500 --> 10:09.800
Ha!

10:09.868 --> 10:11.434
You think that's funny, chief?
Well, I...

10:11.502 --> 10:12.901
My wife is dead.

10:12.969 --> 10:15.002
Oh, I'm... I'm sorry.

10:15.070 --> 10:16.870
She's dead, chief.
Ho-ho! Dead.

10:16.937 --> 10:19.837
The Grateful Dead. Please
do not take the brown acid.

10:19.905 --> 10:21.657
It will turn you
into a Martian.

10:21.725 --> 10:23.457
Take me to your wiener.
Ho-ho!

10:23.524 --> 10:26.125
We're (bleep).

10:26.193 --> 10:28.827
("Rockin' Robin"
by Bobby Day playing)

10:31.429 --> 10:33.379
♪ ♪

10:37.681 --> 10:39.998
♪ He rocks in the treetop
all a day long ♪

10:40.049 --> 10:42.482
♪ Hoppin' and a-boppin'
and a-singin' the song ♪

10:42.550 --> 10:45.502
♪ All the little birds
on Jaybird Street ♪

10:45.570 --> 10:48.019
♪ Love to hear the robin
goin' tweet-tweet-tweet ♪

10:48.087 --> 10:50.304
♪ Rockin' robin,
tweet-tweet-tweet. ♪

10:52.923 --> 10:55.006
I don't know, Peter.
This all seems kind of creepy.

10:55.074 --> 10:56.758
What do you mean?
This is great!

10:56.826 --> 10:58.592
Everyone's hilarious now!

10:58.660 --> 11:00.426
What do you think, Quagmire?

11:00.493 --> 11:02.779
What? I can't hear a thing
over this noise.

11:02.804 --> 11:03.277
What?!

11:03.278 --> 11:04.879
This is unbearable!

11:04.947 --> 11:07.313
I think I got just the thing
to cheer you up, Joe.

11:07.364 --> 11:10.815
I know I said I was a leg man,
but this is ridiculous. Ho!

11:10.883 --> 11:12.682
I feel like a testicle
on steroids.

11:12.750 --> 11:14.649
Honey, I shrunk my nuts!
Ho! Ha!

11:14.717 --> 11:16.452
Ho-ho! I'm a
San Francisco pirate.

11:16.520 --> 11:18.986
I Haight my Ashbury
in these jeans!

11:19.054 --> 11:21.070
A lot of the material
is repeated.

11:24.723 --> 11:26.056
Mmm, Lois,

11:26.124 --> 11:29.392
your torso is
so broad and solid.

11:30.460 --> 11:32.493
(spits, coughs)

11:32.560 --> 11:33.644
Ah! You're not Lois!

11:33.711 --> 11:35.978
I can hear you!
I'm not deaf!

11:36.046 --> 11:38.730
I don't believe that's
real sign language!

11:38.798 --> 11:40.548
Brian, this is
a disaster!

11:40.615 --> 11:42.098
I turned everyone
into Robin Williams!

11:42.166 --> 11:43.716
You gotta help me!

11:43.784 --> 11:44.882
Yo-yo-yo! Peter G.

11:44.967 --> 11:47.083
What's happening,
dawg?

11:47.151 --> 11:49.336
Oh, Sideways Hat Robin.
Dear God, no!

11:49.387 --> 11:51.337
(kettle whistles)

11:51.388 --> 11:55.422
♪ Gonna have some hot tea,
baby, this morning! ♪

11:55.490 --> 11:56.722
(yells)

11:56.807 --> 11:58.640
Run, Forrest, run!
Run, Forrest, run!

11:58.707 --> 12:00.257
All right, Rupert,
all we have to do

12:00.325 --> 12:01.560
is act like Robin Williams,

12:01.644 --> 12:03.526
and he'll think
we've already changed.

12:03.594 --> 12:04.960
Ho-ho! Scattered
stream of references!

12:05.028 --> 12:07.195
Lots of energy! One good one
for every ten! Ho-ho!

12:11.731 --> 12:14.216
Damn these hands!

12:14.284 --> 12:15.916
Mwah!

12:15.984 --> 12:18.217
Vell, I haven't been
to temple in a while!

12:18.268 --> 12:19.918
Ah!

12:19.986 --> 12:21.652
Ladies and gentleman,
The Doors!

12:21.719 --> 12:24.054
(screaming)

12:24.105 --> 12:26.072
Ho-ho! Jogging!
Running on empty! Ho-ho!

12:26.157 --> 12:27.822
Run, Forrest, run!

12:27.889 --> 12:30.574
ALL:
Ho-ho! Ho-ho! Ho-ho!

12:30.658 --> 12:32.641
Ho-ho! I'm a Mercedes!

12:32.709 --> 12:33.942
Und vere are your papers?

12:34.009 --> 12:36.010
Are you from
East or Vest Berlin?

12:36.078 --> 12:38.745
(a la John Wayne):
Vell, I'm from Vest Berlin, pilgrim.

12:38.813 --> 12:41.480
(sobbing)

12:41.547 --> 12:42.830
Shut up!

12:42.898 --> 12:44.198
(yelling)

12:44.249 --> 12:47.249
(sobbing)

12:47.333 --> 12:49.733
Ho-ho! Ho-ho!
Ho-ho! Ho-ho!

12:49.785 --> 12:52.052
Stop riffing!

12:54.954 --> 12:56.372
Jump, Forest, jump!

12:56.423 --> 12:57.856
Must be a leap
year, ho-ho!

13:04.559 --> 13:06.509
Time to lose
some weight, dearie?

13:06.577 --> 13:09.611
No... more... comedy.

13:15.248 --> 13:16.881
Guys, will you please
settle down?

13:16.932 --> 13:18.415
Can we, can we settle down,
please?

13:18.466 --> 13:19.733
Every... everyone.

13:19.801 --> 13:21.134
Everyone, can I have
your attention?

13:21.202 --> 13:22.535
Oh, Captains! My Captains!

13:22.603 --> 13:25.586
I have an announcement to make:

13:25.654 --> 13:27.086
You are all free!

13:27.154 --> 13:29.155
You have been fired
from the school.

13:29.223 --> 13:32.907
Vietnam is over.
The hospital is closing.

13:32.975 --> 13:34.941
Will Hunting is all better.

13:35.009 --> 13:36.609
It's not your fault.
It's not your fault.

13:36.676 --> 13:38.743
Shut up. Seriously, shut up.

13:38.811 --> 13:40.244
Please, you are done here.

13:40.311 --> 13:43.546
Go and spread your comedy
to all corners of this country.

13:46.148 --> 13:48.048
Wait, not you five.

13:48.116 --> 13:51.250
I'm gonna keep you for...
an experiment.

13:52.986 --> 13:54.286
Ho-ho! Eggs!

13:54.353 --> 13:56.136
Who came first, the chicken
or the porn star?

13:56.204 --> 13:57.236
<i>Ho-ho!
The Porn Identity!</i>

13:57.304 --> 13:58.537
Who am I? Oh, yeah!
The pizza man!

13:58.605 --> 14:00.772
Baka-chikka-bwow-bwow!
Ho-ho! Ho-ho!

14:00.840 --> 14:02.038
Peter, can you pass
the coffee?

14:02.105 --> 14:04.740
Sure, Brian the dog.

14:04.808 --> 14:09.659
Anything for my family.

14:09.743 --> 14:11.827
Coffee now.
Here we go, here we go.

14:14.913 --> 14:17.780
<i>I guess Disney wouldn't let us
do the Aladdin one.</i>

14:27.231 --> 14:30.165
LOIS:
Stewie, rise and shine.

14:32.334 --> 14:34.767
Good morning, Stewie.

14:34.834 --> 14:36.035
(bleep) you.

14:36.102 --> 14:38.220
You ready for the day, sweetie?

14:38.288 --> 14:40.587
Oh, someone needs
a diaper change.

14:46.257 --> 14:47.590
Are you proud
of yourself?

14:47.641 --> 14:48.943
That this
is what you do?

14:49.010 --> 14:51.060
Is this a dime?
Did you swallow a dime?

14:51.127 --> 14:53.578
Yeah, wipe it off
and put it back in your purse,

14:53.645 --> 14:54.945
you white trash hen.

14:55.012 --> 14:56.179
There we go.

14:56.247 --> 14:58.763
Who's my clean little boy?

14:58.814 --> 15:00.281
(Stewie laughing)

15:02.266 --> 15:03.733
Ugh! Your roots
are ridiculous.

15:03.800 --> 15:04.883
I'm gonna grab
your hair 'cause

15:04.951 --> 15:06.017
I like grabbing stuff.

15:06.085 --> 15:08.452
Okay. Okay, Stewie, let go.

15:08.537 --> 15:10.637
Let, let go, Stewie.
Let go of Mommy's hair.

15:10.704 --> 15:12.838
When I grow up, I'm
never gonna call you.

15:12.906 --> 15:15.106
I'm gonna be busy
with my job and my family.

15:15.173 --> 15:16.839
You'll be nothing.

15:21.578 --> 15:24.777
Stewie, I want you
to have my ring.

15:24.828 --> 15:26.596
It's one of my most
important possessions,

15:26.663 --> 15:28.463
and I want you to have it.

15:28.531 --> 15:31.097
Okay, red flag.
Red flag, everybody!

15:35.250 --> 15:37.250
Hey, Stewie,
wanna go down the slide?

15:37.301 --> 15:38.902
STEWIE:
Um...

15:38.970 --> 15:40.102
What's the matter?

15:40.170 --> 15:41.969
Ya never been down
the slide before?

15:42.036 --> 15:43.905
(scoffs) Yeah, like,
like a thousand times.

15:43.973 --> 15:47.139
Just done it so much
I'm bored with it, that's all.

15:49.125 --> 15:51.609
All right, I guess
we're doing this.

15:55.144 --> 15:56.144
Whoa.

15:56.212 --> 15:57.895
Come on down,
Stewie!

15:57.963 --> 16:00.179
(hawks screeching)

16:00.263 --> 16:03.665
This is crazy. This is crazy.
This is crazy.

16:03.732 --> 16:07.600
All right, you can do this,
Stewie. Here we go.

16:07.668 --> 16:08.668
(screams)

16:08.735 --> 16:10.552
(thud)

16:10.620 --> 16:11.586
Are you okay?

16:11.653 --> 16:13.052
Yeah, that wasn't so bad.

16:13.120 --> 16:14.486
You might wanna move.

16:14.554 --> 16:16.687
That farting Polish kid
is coming down the slide.

16:16.772 --> 16:18.522
(Stewie grunts)
(kid farts)

16:18.590 --> 16:19.956
Ah, Pavel!

16:36.116 --> 16:38.249
Hey, kid, come here.
I wanna see

16:38.317 --> 16:40.618
if I can still smell
your mom's boobs on your mouth.

16:40.686 --> 16:42.836
Why don't you go hump
a pile of garbage?

16:46.921 --> 16:49.372
All right, here we go.
Classic.

16:49.456 --> 16:50.773
(engine starts)

16:50.841 --> 16:52.374
Uh-oh. (grunts)

16:56.159 --> 16:57.542
Oh, God! Brian! Brian!

16:59.711 --> 17:02.129
Guess I'm going for a ride.

17:10.000 --> 17:11.334
Why are we stopping?

17:11.401 --> 17:12.484
(squirrel chitters)

17:12.551 --> 17:15.168
Oh, come on.

17:15.220 --> 17:19.821
For God's sake, Brian.
It's just a squirrel.

17:19.889 --> 17:21.022
BRIAN:
Yeah!

17:21.106 --> 17:22.138
Oh, God!

17:26.427 --> 17:27.892
(Stewie groans)

17:27.960 --> 17:29.860
He can't hurt you anymore.

17:34.396 --> 17:35.964
Hey there, little fella.

17:36.032 --> 17:38.565
We sure got a lovely day for it,
don't we?

17:38.633 --> 17:40.432
Stay away from
my brother's butt.

17:42.200 --> 17:45.318
Okay, Stewie, let's get
that little face washed off.

17:45.386 --> 17:47.553
Then you can play
with your bath toys, huh?

17:47.621 --> 17:49.604
No, I hate getting
my face washed!

17:49.672 --> 17:51.406
Oh, look!
It's just Mr. Frog!

17:51.473 --> 17:53.322
Hello, Mr. Frog...

17:53.390 --> 17:54.572
(spluttering)

17:54.657 --> 17:57.057
My God, how the hell
do I keep falling for that?

17:57.125 --> 17:58.742
Now you play with your toys

17:58.810 --> 18:01.361
and I'll go get yo
a nice, fluffy towel.

18:01.428 --> 18:05.328
Stewart Griffin, explorer,
adventurer,

18:05.396 --> 18:07.546
skin-diving
international playboy.

18:07.631 --> 18:09.632
(takes deep breath)

18:11.666 --> 18:14.033
(Stewie growls, screams)

18:14.084 --> 18:15.918
I'm swimming at night
'cause I'm a slut

18:16.003 --> 18:18.252
and now I'm paying
the price for it.

18:18.320 --> 18:20.704
(panting)

18:20.755 --> 18:22.505
Hey, Stewie!

18:22.573 --> 18:25.039
Wow, looks like you got
some cool bath toys in there.

18:25.107 --> 18:26.840
Is it okay if I join ya?

18:26.891 --> 18:28.508
No! (screams)

18:30.977 --> 18:33.044
Hey, is that
my froggie butt cloth?

18:35.879 --> 18:38.630
Okay, Stewie, bedtime's
in ten minutes.

18:38.698 --> 18:39.963
I'll be right back.

18:41.282 --> 18:43.016
Hmm. I think I have time
for a quickie.

18:52.554 --> 18:54.238
Excuse me, Mr. Cobain.

18:54.306 --> 18:55.405
Look, I know
you're depressed.

18:55.473 --> 18:57.673
Made some bad choices
with women,

18:57.741 --> 18:58.957
but there's another way.

18:59.025 --> 19:01.541
Haagen-Dazs,
lots of Haagen-Dazs.

19:04.862 --> 19:05.945
(whooshing)

19:06.013 --> 19:07.495
Well, let's see if it worked.

19:07.562 --> 19:09.029
Here we go.

19:09.096 --> 19:11.747
Ha! You're still alive,
you fat (bleep).

19:11.815 --> 19:13.997
Okay, Stewie, time for bed.

19:14.065 --> 19:16.084
You want Mommy to read you
a night-night story?

19:16.151 --> 19:18.051
Oh, how 'bout this one?

19:18.119 --> 19:22.002
<i>"Good Night, Town
from Footloose"?</i>

19:22.070 --> 19:24.437
LOIS:

19:28.574 --> 19:30.174
Who is this book for?

19:37.946 --> 19:40.346
(slurring): Hey, Lois.
I'm home from the Clam.

19:40.413 --> 19:42.097
You know what that means.

19:42.181 --> 19:45.064
STEWIE: You spent the last ten minutes
parked in front of the house

19:45.132 --> 19:46.615
crying in your car?

19:46.683 --> 19:49.217
Not now, Peter. I'm doing
story time with Stewie.

19:49.285 --> 19:50.485
Yeah, scram, Drinky.

19:50.553 --> 19:51.851
I got a story.

19:51.919 --> 19:54.353
It's about the little penis
that could.

19:54.421 --> 19:56.454
It thinks it can, it thinks...

19:56.522 --> 19:58.221
In fact, it's pretty sure
it can.

19:58.289 --> 19:59.689
It-It, it's gonna.

19:59.756 --> 20:01.224
Hey, am I gonna have
to handle this?

20:01.275 --> 20:02.742
Do you want me
to handle this?

20:02.809 --> 20:03.742
Peter, just go wait
in the bedroom.

20:03.809 --> 20:05.359
I'll be right there.

20:05.426 --> 20:09.194
Fine, but if I gotta pee first,
this night's gonna be ruined.

20:09.261 --> 20:10.478
Ruined.

20:14.431 --> 20:16.281
Good night, sweetie.
Mommy loves you.

20:20.601 --> 20:23.269
(Stewie yawns)

20:23.336 --> 20:24.903
(rhythmic thudding)

20:24.970 --> 20:26.437
Huh?

20:29.489 --> 20:31.022
(both grunting)

20:32.524 --> 20:34.358
It's big, isn't it?

20:34.425 --> 20:36.392
Yes, Peter.
It's very big.

20:36.459 --> 20:40.078
Yeah, it's big.

20:40.129 --> 20:42.461
Oh, God, yes!

20:42.529 --> 20:44.463
Ah, yes...

20:44.548 --> 20:46.648
Ah, yeah.

20:50.000 --> 20:54.009
Oh, you're gonna use that thing,
good. I love you so much.

20:54.010 --> 21:55.010
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru